The calling code below never mentions a concrete class — it depends only on the `PaymentProcessor` contract:

```java
interface PaymentProcessor {
    void charge(double amount);
}

class StripeProcessor implements PaymentProcessor {
    public void charge(double amount) {
        // call Stripe's API
    }
}

class Checkout {
    private final PaymentProcessor processor;

    Checkout(PaymentProcessor processor) {
        this.processor = processor;
    }

    void completeOrder(double total) {
        processor.charge(total);
    }
}

Checkout checkout = new Checkout(new StripeProcessor());
```

Swap `new StripeProcessor()` for `new PayPalProcessor()` and `Checkout` doesn't change at all — it was never coupled to Stripe, only to the `charge(amount)` contract every processor must satisfy.
